/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt-700-Note:
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt:701:While you can toggle between the open and closed states of non-modal dialog boxes by toggling the presence of the open attribute, this approach is not recommended. See open for more information.
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt-702-
--
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt-705-
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt:706:The HTML <dialog> element is used to create both modal and non-modal dialog boxes.
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt:707:Modal dialog boxes block interaction with other UI elements, making the rest of the page inert, while non-modal dialog boxes allow interaction with the rest of the page.
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt-708-
--
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt-712-JavaScript can be used to display and close the <dialog> element.
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt:713:You can use the showModal() method to display a modal dialog and the show() method to display a non-modal dialog. The dialog box can be closed using the close() method or using the dialog method when submitting a <form> that is nested within the <dialog> element.
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt-714-Modal dialogs can also be closed by pressing the Esc key.
