/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt-730-
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt:731:Non-modal dialogs using popover commands
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt-732-
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt:733:Non-modal dialogs can be declaratively opened, closed, and toggled using the Popover API HTML attributes popovertarget and popovertargetaction, which can be defined on <button> and <input> elements.
/workspace/A111/runs/future/versioned_preset_catalog/research/worker/source_snapshots/mdn_dialog.txt-734-The <dialog> must be turned into a popover by adding the popover attribute.
